{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfi6Hou6qTamsvpNGCjk6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016HW3wBBKuoLz5uBmHH1zEf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -i '' \"1613s/let seen/const seen/;1629s/let seen/const seen/\" test/index.ts && cat >> AGENTS.md <<'EOF'\n\n### Prop accessors (`src/factory.ts`)\n\nEach declared prop gets an accessor on the element prototype. Setup's\n`ctx.props.<name>` is a wrapper that reads a bound external signal when\none is assigned, else the host's own signal. Any function assigned to the\naccessor is treated as a signal, so a `p.prop()` holding a function value\ncannot be set through the accessor. While bound, attribute changes are\nignored. Properties set before upgrade are own properties that shadow\nthe accessor; the constructor deletes and re-assigns them. Type side:\n`MicrotagHost<Props>` in `builders.ts` is the instance type of\n`MicrotagElementClass`, and the accessors are typed as the prop value\nonly (mapped types cannot split read and write types).\nEOF\nnpm run lint 2>&1 | grep -c \"error  \"; npm test 2>&1 | grep -c \"^not ok\"; npm run test:ssr 2>&1 | grep -E \"^# (pass|fail)\"; npm run size 2>&1 | grep -ci exceed\ngit add -A && git commit -qm \"Add prop accessors on hosts\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git status --short"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":484,"cache_read_input_tokens":72067,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":484},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3db253de-4327-44c9-a21c-8793264b0323","uuid":"3d9fb55e-96e5-4db3-9201-6f4c02311c6a","timestamp":"2026-10-04T23:49:14.743Z","reques